course: dictionary
lesson: 14109
title: The Mesozoic: Age of Dinosaurs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists split Earth's long history into named times, like chapters in a book. The Mesozoic is one of these long times. It lasted from about 252 million to 66 million years ago, and it is often called the Age of Dinosaurs.
explain: Mesozoic is also an adjective, a describing word. «The team found Mesozoic rocks in the cliffs.» Here Mesozoic tells you the rocks come from that long time, so they are very old, from when dinosaurs lived.
explain: Fossils are the clues scientists use. «Mesozoic fossils show that giant reptiles once walked on Earth.» When you read Mesozoic, think of dinosaurs, reptiles and very old rocks.
fact: Mesozoic means belonging to the time of Earth's history from about 252 million to 66 million years ago.
fact: The Mesozoic is often called the Age of Dinosaurs.
fact: The Mesozoic is split into three periods: the Triassic, the Jurassic and the Cretaceous.
fact: «Mesozoic rocks» are rocks formed during that long time.
fact: The Mesozoic ended when an asteroid hit Earth, and most dinosaurs died out.
exercise: «The team found Mesozoic rocks in the cliffs.» What does Mesozoic describe here? | *Rocks from the time of the dinosaurs | Rocks from the Ice Age | Rocks from the sea | Rocks from the last ten years
exercise: «The Mesozoic lasted from about 252 million to 66 million years ago.» How long ago did the Mesozoic end? | *66 million years ago | 1,000 years ago | 252 million years ago | 2 million years ago
exercise: Which of these is one of the three periods of the Mesozoic? | Cambrian | Ice Age | *Jurassic | Stone Age
test: «The Mesozoic is often called the Age of Dinosaurs.» What is the Mesozoic often called? | The Age of Mammals | The Ice Age | *The Age of Dinosaurs | The Stone Age
test: What is thought to have ended the Mesozoic era? | A great flood | A volcano in a park | *An asteroid hitting Earth | A very cold winter
exam: Which statement about the Mesozoic is true? | It started 66 million years ago | It is the same as the Stone Age | *It lasted about 186 million years | It lasted only one year
